    "source": "The topic of HIV/AIDS receives much less attention than it did three decades ago, when the disease first cut through the LGBTQ community.",
    "claim": "Questions mentioning HIV or AIDS (excluding hearing aids) number between 5 and 16 per year from 1985 to 1993, peaking at 16 in 1988, and at most 2 per year from 2008 to 2017.",
    "tables": {"d": "data/raw_da_qs.csv"},
